        name: "What is a number grid puzzle?",
        acceptedAnswer: {
          "@type": "Answer",
          text: "A number grid puzzle is any logic puzzle played on a grid of cells that uses numbers as clues or fill values. The grid gives every piece of reasoning a physical address: this cell, this row, this number. Popular examples include Sudoku, Shikaku, Kakuro, Nonograms, KenKen, Slitherlink, Akari, and Hitori. All can be solved through pure deduction, no guessing required."
