      {
        "@type": "Question",
        name: "What's the easiest number grid puzzle to start with?",
        acceptedAnswer: {
          "@type": "Answer",
          text: "Sudoku is the most common starting point because the rules are simple and easy puzzles resolve through basic scanning. If you prefer something more spatial, Shikaku is a great alternative: the rules fit in two sentences and the rectangle-shaping feels creative rather than mechanical. Either way, start with small grids and finish them completely before moving up in size."
